      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-02-01_WidnesExaminer_art0008" n="art0008">
        <p>Ilan SALE, a CAB in fair condition (seized for debt).— 3LtmE-81„ near Edge Hill Station, Liverpool.</p>
        <p>H. EZARD, BUILDER AND CONTRACTOR, FEARNHEAD, WARRINGTON,</p>
        <p>Hstimates-given for Alterations and Repairs of every description (Town and Country). Houses built to tenants' own plans. Jobbing puuctually attended to. Rent and Fire and Life Assurance Agent.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-02-01_WidnesExaminer_art0009" n="art0009">
        <head>By pon I le. 71d per Quarter, 6s. 6d. per Antimn le. 9d per Quarter credit •</head>
        <p>By pon I le. 71d per Quarter, 6s. 6d. per Antimn le. 9d per Quarter credit •</p>
        <p>TREMENDOUS REDUCTIONS.</p>
        <p>GOLDSTONE AND SONS',</p>
        <p>115, 117, 119, OXFORD-STREET (right opposite Al! Sainte* Church), MANCHESTER.</p>
        <p>THE LARGRST AND MOST COMPLETE SHOW OF HOUSEHOLD FURNITURE OUTSIDE LONDON. SECOND-HAND FURNITURE, BEDSTEADS, Ix., &amp;c., BY ALL THE BEST MAKERS, AT2S PER CENT. BELOW COST.</p>
        <p>CONDITIONS OF SALE.—AII Goods packed and de- livered free any distance. Railway fair paid to country customers. Goods stored free of charge until required. All articles re-polished and exchanged if not approved of. • The PUBLIC ARE INVITED TO CALL AND SEE THE WONDERFUL BARGAINS now being offered, the quality of the FURNITURE being A 1, and now sold at Ridiculously Low Prices to make room for several large houses of Furniture now stored away, haying no room to show them. Don't delay, but call at once, and capture the bargains now awaiting you, When you come to visit us you have no ex- pense. We pay your Railway Fares, we Deliver the Goods Free, and you see what you cannot see in .our own town that is £lO.OOO worth of good, substantial New and Second- hand Furniture to Select from. Come to Blanchester by all means, and Save fully 50 per cent of your hard-earned money. GOOD SECOND-HAND FURNITURE IS BETTER THAN</p>
        <p>NEW. THIS WEEK'S BARGAINS IN DINING-ROOM FURNITURE.</p>
        <p>£1 10s. Od., worth £l2 10s. Od., very massive DINING-ROOM SUITE, in leather, large Couch, pair of Easy Chairs, and four smal:s, all made by ,tmith. £1 15s. Od. Very massive Solid Mahogany SIDE- BOARD, with large bevelled glass back and shelves; original:y cost nearly £2O ; just been re-polished. Fitted with drawers and cupboard, and all conveniences. £7 15s. Od., worth £2O. Very heavy DINING- ROOM SUITE, in claret coloured leather, solid frames, and small chairs, padded backs, just been re-upholstered and re-polished. Call and inspect. £7 17s. 6d., cost when new £lB. Handsome SADDLE-BAG SUITE, solid frames, end beautifully uphols- tered Couch, pair of Ladies' and Gents' Easy Chairs, and four small Chairs, all stuffed backs. Delivered free any distance. _ _</p>
        <p>£l4 14s. Od., cost £3O. Grand Bargain in a Secomi-hand Solid Oak DINING-ROOM SUITE, by Radcliffe, consisting of the Couch, two Easy Chairs, and six Standard Padded Back Single Chairs, upholstered irt green Morocco leather, very little worn, in fact as good as new. £2 15s. Od. The massive DINING TABLE to match above suite, beautifully-carved legs, well got up. Cost when new £9. £5 15s. Od. Well worth £2O. The very unique sec*nd-hand solid oak Sideboard, with lofty back, fitted with bevelled silvered plates, fitted with drawers, cupboards, cellerette, and all the modern conveniences. Worthy of attention. .E5O Os. Od. Very massive DINING-ROOM SUITE in real Morocco, upholstered with hair in solid walnut frames, large Couch. two Gentlemen's Easy Chairs and six Standard Chairs, with large stuffed backs, all castored ; 6it. American Walnut Sideboard to match, all silvered plates, bevelled drawers, cupboards, and shelves ; very heavy 6ft. Dining Table with extending screw and loose leaves, the Coal Vase to match. The lot honestly worth £l5O. Delivered and packed free of charge. £1 ss. Oct to £2O. Walnut, oak, mahogany and Cyprus DINING TABLES, in all SinS and makes, to suit everybody, in all sizes to suit every family. and at all prices to suit every pocket. Mind you, all Second-hand, at second- hand Prices.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-02-01_WidnesExaminer_art0010" n="art0010">
        <head>THIS WEEK'S BARGAINS IN DRAWING ROOM FURNITURE.</head>
        <p>THIS WEEK'S BARGAINS IN DRAWING ROOM FURNITURE.</p>
        <p>£3 103. Od., originally cost 16 guineas. Elegant DRAWING-ROOM CABINET, in mid walnut, fitted, cern- plete with beautitully silvered bevelled plates. A noble article. _ _</p>
        <p>£si9. 6d., worth £lO. Nice little DRAWING.. ROOM SUITE, in Freize Velvet. Secondhand, and very little used ; good size Couch. pair of Easy Chairs, and four small Chairs, with padded backs, well upholstered. De-- livered free. _</p>
        <p>XS 15s. Od.. cost when new 25 guineas. Beautiful finished DRAWING-ROOM SUITE, in solid walnut frames, upholsterel in rich brocade, velvet, old gold colour, all large pies a very ';ltle soiled, brass castored. A bargain. £lO 104, worth R-30. Very handsome Chip- dpndate DIU ING-ROOM SUITE, in expensive Genoa vel- vet, nicely el. rved frames and well finished. Consists of Settee, pair or Easy Chairs, and four Occasional Chairs. cheap. ..E0 15s. Od. Second - hand CHIPPENDALE CABINET, t y Ogden. worth £25. Beautifully carved ir bas relief, and II silvered plates bevelled; the underneath portion is fitteu with glass-panelled doors and shelves, for the display of bric•a-brac. Also the CENTRE TABLE, to match, by the same maker, for 275. 6d., worth £3. is. Od. DRAWING-ROOM BRASS SET com- plete, comprising heavy Curb. pair of Fire Dogs. and Set of Fire Brasses, all to match. Honestly worth £2 2s. C.d. Fit any hearth. £3O Os. Od. Very fine rosewood inlaid DRAWING. ROOM SUITE, upholstered in rich Genoa Velvet, with plush border., all hair stuffed. Made by Oetzman. The suite oum- orie 'ery flue double-el&amp; t Settee, elegantly upholstered. pair ot luxurious Easy Chairs, four small Chairs with very fine carved backs, and two small Occasional Chairs with padded backs. Been in use for this season only, and not a bit worse for wear. .E 23 108. Od. Second - hand rosewood inlaid DRAWING-ROOM CABINET, 41t. 6in. wide, with large fancy back glass cupboards each side. Will match the above suite. Octagon Centre Table to match for 305., cost 50s. The inlaid envelope Card Table, also to match for 4 guineas; whets new cost £lO. The rosewood inlaid Over Mantel from the same house, for £3 3s. Od., cost £6 lea. Od. Thiele a very Eno lot, and well worthy of attention. £3 19s. 6d. Complete set of FIRE BRASSES, to- gether with massive Curb, nicely chased, pair of Doge ana Stop. Will fit any ordinary hearth. Well worth £lOl All are well lacquered on church brass.</p>
        <p>THIS WEEK'S BARGAINS IN BEDROOM FURNITURE. £2 10s. Od. The Complete Second-hand Lot of FURNITURE, for Bedroom, consists of large size Dressing Table fitted with chewers ; Swing Glass; Washstand, fitted bottom board and drawers; two Cane Chairs and Towel Rail ; the lot cheap at £5. £5 ss. Od. Very Handsome Solid Walnut Pair of DUCHESSE STANDS. heavy carved legs, fitted with bevelled-plate, and numerous jewel drawers and boxes to Dressing Table, and large marble slab to Washstand, just been re polished, and are equal to flew; well worth £lO. £6 15s. Od., cost when new £2O. The handsomest Pair of TOILET TABLES inManchester. All Solid. Large bevelled silvered glass, all drawers and cupboards in botf,,. real marble slab and tile bask, and bevelled silvered glass in washstand ; all clustered and brass handled.</p>
        <p>XS 15s. Od. Solid Satin Walnut BEDROOM SUITE, comprising large Wardrobe, with silver plate in door ; pair of enclosed Toilet Tables, with towel rail and pot cupboard attached ; two Cane Chairs, just been repolished and overhauled ; made by Herman, worth £25.</p>
        <p>£l3 13s. Od. The 'finest Second-hand SUITE at the price in Manchester. Large size Wardrobe, fitted with drawers and hanging compartment. large bevelled plate in aoor ; pair of well-constructed Toilet Tables,with swing glass to both dressing table and washstand, marble slab and tile back, both on castors; Towel Rail and pedestal Cupboard attached ; and three. Cane Chairs. Well worth £m £l6 16s. Od. ' American walnut BEDROOM SUIT% by Doveston,comprising large Wardrobe, with bevel- led silvered plate in centre door, and large drawer below, inside fitted for hangings, and beautifully lined in sateen ; pair of elegantly-constructed Toilet tables, both fitted with bevelled glass in backs, both fully castored, Towel Rail and pedestal Cupboard combined, and three Cane Chairs. A marvel of cheapness. Hone3tly worth £35. £2O 0. Od. Very fine BEDROOM SUITE in American and Italian walnut; all scud and no worse for wear, The fall complement of pieces. Well finished; worth £4O.</p>
        <p>—.kl7 Os. 01, worth £45. Solid Satin walnut BEDROOM SUITE, same number of p.eces as above Suite, but a bit smaller. Capital value. £9O Os. Od. The entire CONTENTS of a beauti- fully FURNISEIED REDROOM fit to adorn the house of a Duke. The lot consist of a Bedroom Suite that baffles description, made by Hill, of Glasgow. solid American walnut, with Italian walnut panels, large silvered bevel plate In door of Wardrobe, the other doors fitted with transparent bevelled plates, with plush behind, utted with drawers, cup- boards, and nicely lined in sateen to match. The pair of handsome Toilet Tables with side mirror, large swing glass in centre both to dressing table and washstand, three upholster Chairs, Towel Airer, and Bedside Pedestal. Very massive Parisian Bedstead in solid brass square pillars, upholstered in rich French tapestry and plush. The upholstered spring Mattress, hair Overlay, Bolster, and two large feather Pillows, large Carpet, and gilt Chimney Glass. The above was never bought under £250, and is fully worth that amount.</p>
        <p>Bs. 9d. to £25. The FINEST SHOW OF BRASS AND IRON BEDSTEADS IN LANCASHIRE, CHESHIRE, YORKSHIRE and STAFFORDSHIRE. All sizes from 3ft. to sft. 6d., in French, Parisian, Italian walnut and sattn walnut; any price to suit you. You would do well to call and inspect our Bedstead and Bedding Department. It will astonish you and give you some idea Of what we are doing. GOLDSTONE AND SONS'</p>
        <p>SECOND-HAND FURNITURE.</p>
        <p>£l5 worth £5O. Complete House of SECOND-HAND FURNITURB, consisting of parlour, kitchen, and two bed. rooms, everything compete.</p>
        <p>HOUSES COMPLETELY FURNISHED at a FEW HOURS' NOTICE. from £5 to £l,OOO. Corn petent men sent out all over the country to give estimates and fit up. No charge to the purchaser. Clive us a call; we charge nothing for showing you over our vast establishment, and if you don't see anything that will tempt you, you will be more thon hard to please,</p>
        <p>II,AILWAY FARE PAID TO COUNTRY CUSTOMERS.</p>
        <p>NOTE OUE ONLY ADDRESS : THE NOTED HOUSE FURNISHERS, OLDSTON E AND kT SONS', 11,5, 117, 119, OXFORD-STREET, Immediately Opposite All Saints' Church, MANCHESTER. Old Trafford, Brooks' Bar,tralatine-road, and Oxford-street, Irams pass tlie door. Fare Id.;from Market-street.</p>
        <p>MADE-UP DISHES</p>
        <p>Which are a most important gem in the week's menu of every household, are made most piquant and tasty by the addition of</p>
        <p>hich is the</p>
        <p>guaranteed</p>
