        <p>And other internal Alterations, all local and outsida shops will sink to insignificance.</p>
        <p>rilHl4 following will convey but a faint ilea of the Mar- vellous Bargains on yew, any of which may be stored free of charge till required. TERMS oF BUSINESS DURING THE SALE. GOODS EXCHANGND IF NOT SATISFACTORY. EXPERIENCED MEN SENT TO FIX AND FIT UP. GOODS PACKED AND DELIVERED FliHri. CARPETS MADE FREE.</p>
        <p>LOCK-UP STORE ROOMS FOR CONVENIENCE OF CUSTOMERS.</p>
        <p>And, lastly, If you purehase.on my Deferred Payment System</p>
        <p>I Charge a Simple Five per Cent Eitsa. - Every customer attended to by a member of the firm, which prevents the annoyance of a salesmsm who charges high prices in order to make a big commission. Bankers—Manchester Joint-Stock Bank. Telegrams—" Universal," Manchester.</p>
        <p>DURING the Sale, Magnificent Solid Oak DINING- ROWS SUITE. comprising a grand couch, two noble easy chairs, and six superior spoon-back chairs, all in splendid condition, not 'raged; originally cost £55, sale price 9gs. Grand Sideboard to match, 7gs.. worth £4O; Dining Table , to match, 635. In addition to above, we have a truly magnificent Col- lection of Dining-room Suites, over 200, with Sideboards, Dining Tables. and Overmantels to match. An inspection will prove the fact that nowhere can such an assortment be seen except at GERSHON'S, the Universal Furnishing Arcade, 44, Oldham-street, next to the Adelphi Bank, Man- chester. Note.—The above may be had on my deferred payment system for a simple five per cent extra added to invoice. SPECIAL ATTENTIuN to Lot 166. which is in Pollard Oak and without a doubt the best and handsomest it in Man:theater. The Sideboard, which is 7:t. long and very lofty, can only be described as simply magnificent and the most unique in design we have ever seen. The Suite of 12 small chairs (may be had with a less number), two large Lounge Chairs, and large Couch, are all stuffed with hair and covered in morocco leather, guaranteed. The Dining-table, on carved supports, is very handsome, having number of loose leaves. We offer the lot for 145 gs. ; cost over £4OO. We may state that sgs. each will be allowed for any of the small chairs not required. We wish to impress upon the public that every lot advertised is on our premises and hundreds of others. Remember address, GERSHON'S Old-established Universal Furnishing Arcade, 44, Oldham-street (next to the Adelphi Bank), Manchester. Note. —lf on the deferred payment system only five per cent. extra added to invoice.</p>
        <p>OT 237 is in Oriental Saddle Bags, carved walnut frames. L 4 consisting of half-dozen small chairs, two easy chairs, and couch; i rice £25, reduced for the sale to £9 155.. Side- board to match, with bevelled-glass back, a pertect beauty; sale price, £6 155.. usual price 12gs. Dining Table, 38s. 6d. Three other Suites in Saddle Bags, real Persian, everlasting ware, splendid patterns, among which is a water lily, most charming and pleasing ; the wood work in these suites is American walmut, brown oak, and mahogany. and the prices are 18, 25, and 36gs. ; they each cost a;10. £l5, and £25 a suite more. Sideboards, Tables, and Overmantels to match, all on view in our showrooms. Hundreds of other Suites on view. Call and inspect for yourselves ; you will not be un- duly pressed to buy. We have no salesmen or walking gen- tlemen who work for a commission. Every customer is attended to by a member of the firm at GERSHON'S Univer- sal Furnishing Arcade, 44, Oldham-street (next to Adelphi Bank), Manchester. Note.—lf on the deferred payment system only five per cent, extra added to invoice.</p>
        <p>I 0T97 Is Charming DINING-ROOM SUITE, in embosseol LA leather, very handsome and stylish, frame work beauti- fully carved; the six stsndard chairs have padded backs, the two easy chairs are large and comfortable, and the couch is most luxuriously upholstered. This suite is in solid American vrainutwood and is suitable for high-class dining-room. Usual price. 255. ; sale price. 15gs. Another Suite, in Solid Maho,zany. in good hard grain leather. Cromwellian style ; sound in every respect; not soiled. Recently been recovered. A marvel of cheapness ; only 9gs. Another in Walnut. covered in leather, reduced to sgs. Sideboard, to match. 421. ; table, 21s. These bargains are on offer during the sale and before alterations are comraenced. Inspection invited.</p>
        <p>SWEEPING REDUCTIONS. 3f UST CLEAR PREVIOUS TO ALTERATIONS. T OT 51 is a BEDROOM SUITE. Those wishing to furnish IA a bcdroom in high-class style and good taste should I Inspect it, for style, workmanship, and design it cannot ne equalled, the massive large size wardrobe with two bevelled glass doors of rare brilliancy reaching from plinth to cornice : the full-size pedestal dressing table, double washstand to match, pedestal bedside cupboard, towel airer. and three chairs, the whole are in rosewood, richly inlaid with tulip, box, olive, and other rare woods. The cost of this noble Suite was £lOO. bale price 55gs. Another Suite in walnut cost £125 for 60gs , and another in Spanish mahogany cost £55 for 27gs. Special attention is requested to Lots 6,7, 8 and 9, which are Suites in walnut, silver birch, mahogany, and ash, each Suite hasa large wardrobe, with Levelled glass door : dressing table with large la •yelled glass attached, supported by carved brackets restingon raised jewel drawers; it also forms a chest of drawers, being enclosed by four drawers; the large wash staiad is also enclosed, and has a marble slab, tile back, and bevelled shaving glass above, towel rail, pedestal beeiside cupboard, and three chairs. These suite ate guaranteed solid, no veneer being used. S,le price, 151 gs. Other suites smaller from £4 15s, inspection Invited. Any of the abov may be stored free of charge V', required.</p>
