        <p>MACKENZIE'S FEMALE REMEDY. One case guaranteed to remove the most OBSTINATE OBsTRUCTICNS and IRREGULARITIK'S in 12 hours HARMLESS. Nothing can resist it. Failure is impossible Seed stamped envelope for PARTICULARS. TESTI- MONIALS. and ADVICE.. Ours is the most POWERFUL and STRONGEST Remedy Sold, and in no single case has it ever failed—even in the m )st longstanding, intricate, snd lingering cases. Post free, under cover, with written guarantee of cure be. (five shillings),—Mrs. W. E. MACKENZIE, Trafford House, 83, Dawes-roacl, Fulham, London. Mention paper.</p>
        <p>Rail BRITAIN' ISOLATION.</p>
        <p>The desire or foreigners to make political capital out of the insults offered to, this country*, has, been largely discounted by the formation of the Flying Squadron. The energy tits- playel by the War Office and the Admiralty has nippe&amp; in the bud the growing impertinence of our envious competi- tors. The competition in trade by Great Eritain in all the markets of the world is perhaps the secret cause of foreign hate. Nothing arouses envy so much as successful competi- tion in business. Great Britain is the most successful of all the traders of the earth, hence the wreathing of her enemies. A parallel case exist in this city of Manchester. Worsley,the Greatest House Furnisher in the North of England and one of the most successful competitors in the trade of this great City, is the subject of envy and jealousy amongst his would- her competitors. Worsley's reply:to these jealous competitors is to organise a Flying Squadron of Marvellous Bargain which will obliterate and pulverise any possible retaliation.</p>
        <p>THE FLYING SQUADRON OF BARGAINS IS NOW ON VLEVir AT W ORSLEY'S BIG</p>
        <p>" THB PATHEON." GAYTHORN. MANCHNSTBIt.</p>
        <p>Is filled to overflowing with countless and innnrisenthl hosts of Wonderful and Extraordinary Bargains. The vast building of the Pantheon is open to all for inspection.. Yon can walk in with perfect freedom, inspect the stock, please yourself whether you buy or not. All requiring cheap lots in furnishing should inspect Worsley's befoLe deciding. We in- vite comparison of prices, quantity, and quality.</p>
