        <p>WARRINGTON. LIBERAL ASSOCIATION - ANNUAL MEETING. The annual meeting of this association was held' last night, Councillor Pierpoint, J.P. in the A vote of condolence was passed to the Queen sou' royal family on their recent bereavement. MI-- John Rylands, J.P., was re-elected president, Mr. C. Jackson Holmes, hon. treasurer, and Councillor Roberts, J.P., hon. sec. The vice-presidents and. co-optative members on the general Council of the executive were also elected. With reference to the recent criticism in the press, a very kindly invita— tion was given to the writers to communicate to the officers of the Association any suggestions they' may have to make with reference to the party. The Liberal soiree and dance which .will be held oa February 11th, was Leartily taken up by the mem.. bers and is likely to be a great success.. It was announced tkat Mr. Scott's health had improved, and he expects that a journey to the East which he is about to make, will completely restore him.</p>
